      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Corydoras (lineage 5) cf. elegans</li><li>Common name: San Juan Cory</li><li>Pronunciation: kor ee doh rass (lineage five)</li><li>Etymology: Cory = helmet, doras = skin. In this case it was incorrectly used to mean armour (cuirasse) instead of skin in allusion to the dual rows of plates that run along the flanks of this genus.</li></ul>"
